\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Convergent nocuity. (a)~Among majority-convergent violations ($\geq $3/5 models), 77\% reflect permissive interpretation; authorization scope shows near-universal permissive bias (99\%), while conditional precedence splits between permissive and restrictive. (b)~Pairwise Jaccard similarity of violation clause sets: cross-family mean (0.46) approaches within-family levels (0.54; dashed box), convergence reflects shared architectural biases rather than training-data overlap.}}{8}{figure.caption.20}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:convergent_nocuity}{{6}{8}{Convergent nocuity. (a)~Among majority-convergent violations ($\geq $3/5 models), 77\% reflect permissive interpretation; authorization scope shows near-universal permissive bias (99\%), while conditional precedence splits between permissive and restrictive. (b)~Pairwise Jaccard similarity of violation clause sets: cross-family mean (0.46) approaches within-family levels (0.54; dashed box), convergence reflects shared architectural biases rather than training-data overlap}{figure.caption.20}{}}
